# Normalize line endings so `git diff` / `git status` only ever
# show real content changes — not line-ending noise.
#
# Without this, files checked out with CRLF (\r\n) endings on one
# machine and LF (\n) on another look 100% "modified" to git even
# when nothing in the actual code changed, which is what made this
# repo's diffs unreadable and broke a `git am` patch apply.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff2 binary
